# Copilot Instructions

## ConnectAPA
These instructions apply when generating or modifying code in the `ConnectAPA` project.

`ConnectAPA` is responsible only for communicating with the APA GraphQL API.

- Endpoint: `https://gql.poolplayers.com/graphql`
- Do not generate SQL, Entity Framework, or CueConnect application logic in this project.

---

## Core Requirements
- Use `HttpClient` for all HTTP communication.
- Send all GraphQL requests to `https://gql.poolplayers.com/graphql`.
- APA requires batched GraphQL requests, even for a single operation.
- Always send requests as a JSON array of `GraphQlRequest` objects.
- Always include the header `Authorization: Bearer {token}`.
- If no bearer token is available, fail fast instead of sending the request anonymously.
- Store GraphQL queries in `.graphql` files under `GraphQL/Queries/`.
- Load raw GraphQL text from those `.graphql` files.
- Do not hardcode GraphQL query strings in C# unless explicitly requested.
- Use `System.Text.Json` for serialization and deserialization.
- Do not use `GraphQL.Client`.
- Do not use `Newtonsoft.Json`.
- Do not attempt schema introspection. APA blocks it.

